    <summary><span class="faq-label">Drawdown Rules</span><span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
    </summary>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="acc-intro">At Forge of Traders, we use a transparent risk model that combines a <strong>Daily limit</strong> with an <strong>Overall (Static) limit</strong> to give you clear boundaries for your trading.</p>

      <div class="desc-blocks">
        <div class="desc-block">
          <div class="desc-block-title">Daily Drawdown (EOD Balance-Based)</div>
          <p>The Daily Drawdown is a limit that resets every day at the close of the trading session. Because it recalculates based on your closing performance, it is not static.</p>
          <ul class="rule-list">
            <li><strong>The Reset Time:</strong> The daily cycle resets at <strong>21:00 UTC</strong> (Server Time).</li>
            <li><strong>The Calculation:</strong> The limit is calculated based on your End-of-Day (EOD) Balance at the moment of the 21:00 UTC reset.</li>
            <li><strong>The Limit:</strong> Typically <strong>5%</strong> (please verify your specific challenge tier).</li>
            <li><strong>The Floor:</strong> Every evening at 21:00 UTC, your daily "hard floor" is recalculated for the next 24 hours. For example, if your balance is $102,000 at the reset, your floor for the next day is $102,000 minus 5%.</li>
            <li><strong>The Breach:</strong> A breach occurs if your Current Balance (including floating P&amp;L) touches this calculated floor at any point before the next reset.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="desc-block">
          <div class="desc-block-title">Overall Drawdown (Static)</div>
          <p>During the evaluation stages, your Maximum (Overall) Drawdown is <strong>Static</strong>, meaning it is anchored to a fixed point and does not "chase" your profits.</p>
          <ul class="rule-list">
            <li><strong>The Calculation:</strong> It is calculated once based on your <strong>Initial Account Balance</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Fixed Floor:</strong> If you have a $100,000 account with a 10% Max Drawdown, your floor is $90,000.</li>
            <li><strong>Consistency:</strong> This floor remains at $90,000 regardless of how much profit you generate. Even if your account balance grows to $109,000, your absolute floor stays at $90,000.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="desc-block">
          <div class="desc-block-title">The Balance Lock (Funded Accounts Only)</div>
          <p>The Balance Lock is a milestone for Funded Traders that secures your account once you have proven your consistency.</p>
          <ul class="rule-list">
            <li><strong>The 10% Target:</strong> Once your Funded Account reaches a Balance Lock Target of <strong>10% profit</strong>, the lock is triggered.</li>
            <li><strong>One-Time Adjustment:</strong> At this point, your Static Max Drawdown floor is moved one time to your <strong>Initial Account Balance</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Indefinite Security:</strong> Once moved to the Initial Balance, the floor stays there indefinitely. This ensures you are trading with your "profit buffer," and the account is only suspended if your balance returns to your starting balance.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

